 0$.\n\nCRT: $F \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$, $F \\equiv 76 \\pmod{125}$.\n\n$76 \\mod 4 = 0$. So $F = 76$ works? Check: $76 \\mod 4 = 0$ ✓, $76 \\mod 125 = 76$ ✓. So $F = 76 \\mod 500$.\n\nWait, but we need $F \\mod 500$. The solution is $F \\equiv 76 \\pmod{500}$? Let me verify: $76 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$ ✓ and $76 \\equiv 76 \\pmod{125}$ ✓. Yes, $F \\equiv 76 \\pmod{500}$.\n\nSo $F = 2016^{2016} \\equiv 76 \\pmod{500}$.\n\nNow back to $E \\mod 625$: $E \\mod 625 = 2016^{F} \\mod 625 = 2016^{76} \\mod 625$ (since $F \\equiv 76 \\pmod{500}$ and we reduce exponent mod $\\phi(625)=500$).\n\nWait, actually we need $2016^{2016^{2016}} \\mod 625$. The exponent is $2016^{2016}$, and we reduce it mod $\\phi(625) = 500$. We found $2016^{2016} \\equiv 76 \\pmod{500}$. So $2016^{2016^{2016}} \\equiv 2016^{76} \\pmod{625}$.\n\n$2016 \\mod 625 = 2016 - 3 \\cdot 625 = 2016 - 1875 = 141$.\n\nSo compute $141^{76} \\mod 625$.\n\nLet me compute this step by step using repeated squaring.\n\n$141^1 = 141$.\n$141^2 = 19881$. $19881 \\mod 625$: $625 \\cdot 31 = 19375$. $19881 - 19375 = 506$. So $141^2 \\equiv 506 \\pmod{625}$.\n\n$141^4 \\equiv 506^2 = 256036 \\pmod{625}$. $625 \\cdot 409 = 255625$. $256036 - 255625 = 411$. So $141^4 \\equiv 411$.\n\n$141^8 \\equiv 411^2 = 168921 \\pmod{625}$. $625 \\cdot 270 = 168750$. $168921 - 168750 = 171$. So $141^8 \\equiv 171$.\n\n$141^{16} \\equiv 171^2 = 29241 \\pmod{625}$. $625 \\cdot 46 = 28750$. $29241 - 28750 = 491$. So $141^{16} \\equiv 491$.\n\n$141^{32} \\equiv 491^2 = 241081 \\pmod{625}$. $625 \\cdot 385 = 240625$. $241081 - 240625 = 456$. So $141^{32} \\equiv 456$.\n\n$141^{64} \\equiv 456^2 = 207936 \\pmod{625}$. $625 \\cdot 332 = 207500$. $207936 - 207500 = 436$. So $141^{64} \\equiv 436$.\n\nNow $76 = 64 + 8 + 4$. So $141^{76} = 141^{64} \\cdot 141^8 \\cdot 141^4 \\equiv 436 \\cdot 171 \\cdot 411 \\pmod{625}$.\n\nFirst, $436 \\cdot 171 = 74556$. $74556 \\mod 625$: $625 \\cdot 119 = 74375$. $74556 - 74375 = 181$. So $\\equiv 181$.\n\nThen $181 \\cdot 411 = 74391$. $74391 \\mod 625$: $625 \\cdot 119 = 74375$. $74391 - 74375 = 16$. So $\\equiv 16$.\n\nSo $E \\mod 625 = 16$.\n\nAnd $E \\mod 4 = 0$.\n\nCRT for $E \\mod 2500$: $E \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$, $E \\equiv 16 \\pmod{625}$.\n\n$16 \\mod 4 = 0$ ✓. So $E \\equiv 16 \\pmod{2500}$.\n\nSo $E = 2016^{2016^{2016}} \\equiv 16 \\pmod{2500}$.\n\nNow the main computation mod 3125: $2016^{2016^{2016^{2016}}} \\equiv 2016^{E} \\pmod{3125}$, where $E \\equiv 16 \\pmod{2500}$.\n\nSo $2016^{2016^{2016^{2016}}} \\equiv 2016^{16} \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$2016 \\mod 3125 = 2016$.\n\nCompute $2016^{16} \\mod 3125$.\n\n$2016^2 = 4064256$. $4064256 \\mod 3125$: $3125 \\cdot 1300 = 4062500$. $4064256 - 4062500 = 1756$. So $2016^2 \\equiv 1756$.\n\n$2016^4 \\equiv 1756^2 = 3083536 \\pmod{3125}$. $3125 \\cdot 986 = 3081250$. $3083536 - 3081250 = 2286$. So $2016^4 \\equiv 2286$.\n\n$2016^8 \\equiv 2286^2 = 5225796 \\pmod{3125}$. $3125 \\cdot 1672 = 5225000$. $5225796 - 5225000 = 796$. So $2016^8 \\equiv 796$.\n\n$2016^{16} \\equiv 796^2 = 633616 \\pmod{3125}$. $3125 \\cdot 202 = 631250$. $633616 - 631250 = 2366$. So $2016^{16} \\equiv 2366 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nSo $2016^{2016^{2016^{2016}}} \\equiv 2366 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nAnd $\\equiv 0 \\pmod{32}$.\n\nNow CRT: find $x$ such that $x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{32}$ and $x \\equiv 2366 \\pmod{3125}$, with $0 \\le x < 100000$.\n\n$x = 32k$ for some $k$. $32k \\equiv 2366 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nNeed inverse of 32 mod 3125. $3125 = 97 \\cdot 32 + 21$. $32 = 1 \\cdot 21 + 11$. $21 = 1 \\cdot 11 + 10$. $11 = 1 \\cdot 10 + 1$. $10 = 10 \\cdot 1$.\n\nBack-substitute: $1 = 11 - 10 = 11 - (21 - 11) = 2 \\cdot 11 - 21 = 2(32 - 21) - 21 = 2 \\cdot 32 - 3 \\cdot 21 = 2 \\cdot 32 - 3(3125 - 97 \\cdot 32) = 2 \\cdot 32 - 3 \\cdot 3125 + 291 \\cdot 32 = 293 \\cdot 32 - 3 \\cdot 3125$.\n\nSo $32^{-1} \\equiv 293 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nCheck: $32 \\cdot 293 = 9376$. $9376 \\mod 3125$: $3125 \\cdot 3 = 9375$. $9376 - 9375 = 1$ ✓.\n\nSo $k \\equiv 293 \\cdot 2366 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$293 \\cdot 2366 = 293 \\cdot 2000 + 293 \\cdot 366 = 586000 + 107238 = 693238$.\n\n$693238 \\mod 3125$: $3125 \\cdot 221 = 690625$. $693238 - 690625 = 2613$. So $k \\equiv 2613 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$k = 2613$, $x = 32 \\cdot 2613 = 83616$.\n\nCheck: $83616 < 100000$ ✓.\n\nVerify: $83616 \\mod 32 = 0$ ✓ (since $83616 = 32 \\cdot 2613$).\n\n$83616 \\mod 3125$: $3125 \\cdot 26 = 81250$. $83616 - 81250 = 2366$ ✓.\n\nSo the last five digits are $\\boxed{83616}$.\n\nLet me double-check the computation of $141^{76} \\mod 625$ more carefully, since that's a critical step.\n\n$141^2 = 19881$. $19881 / 625 = 31.8096$. $31 \\cdot 625 = 19375$. $19881 - 19375 = 506$. ✓\n\n$506^2 = 256036$. $256036 / 625 = 409.657$. $409 \\cdot 625 = 255625$. $256036 - 255625 = 411$. ✓\n\n$411^2 = 168921$. $168921 / 625 = 270.27$. $270 \\cdot 625 = 168750$. $168921 - 168750 = 171$. ✓\n\n$171^2 = 29241$. $29241 / 625 = 46.78$. $46 \\cdot 625 = 28750$. $29241 - 28750 = 491$. ✓\n\n$491^2 = 241081$. $241081 / 625 = 385.73$. $385 \\cdot 625 = 240625$. $241081 - 240625 = 456$. ✓\n\n$456^2 = 207936$. $207936 / 625 = 332.70$. $332 \\cdot 625 = 207500$. $207936 - 207500 = 436$. ✓\n\n$76 = 64 + 8 + 4$. $141^{76} = 141^{64} \\cdot 141^8 \\cdot 141^4 = 436 \\cdot 171 \\cdot 411$.\n\n$436 \\cdot 171 = 74556$. $74556 / 625 = 119.29$. $119 \\cdot 625 = 74375$. $74556 - 74375 = 181$. ✓\n\n$181 \\cdot 411 = 74391$. $74391 / 625 = 119.025$. $119 \\cdot 625 = 74375$. $74391 - 74375 = 16$. ✓\n\nGreat, $E \\mod 625 = 16$, and $E \\mod 4 = 0$, so $E \\equiv 16 \\pmod{2500}$.\n\nNow let me also double check $2016^{16} \\mod 3125$.\n\n$2016^2 = 4064256$. $4064256 / 3125 = 1300.56$. $1300 \\cdot 3125 = 4062500$. $4064256 - 4062500 = 1756$. ✓\n\n$1756^2 = 3083536$. $3083536 / 3125 = 986.73$. $986 \\cdot 3125 = 3081250$. $3083536 - 3081250 = 2286$. ✓\n\n$2286^2 = 5225796$. $5225796 / 3125 = 1672.25$. $1672 \\cdot 3125 = 5225000$. $5225796 - 5225000 = 796$. ✓\n\n$796^2 = 633616$. $633616 / 3125 = 202.76$. $202 \\cdot 3125 = 631250$. $633616 - 631250 = 2366$. ✓\n\nSo the answer is 83616.\n\nLet me also verify the chain of exponent reductions is correct.\n\nWe want $N = 2016^{2016^{2016^{2016}}} \\mod 100000$.\n\n$100000 = 32 \\cdot 3125$, $\\gcd(32, 3125) = 1$.\n\n**Mod 32:** $2016 = 32 \\cdot 63 \\equiv 0$. The exponent $2016^{2016^{2016}}$ is certainly $\\geq 5$ (it's astronomically large), so $0^{\\text{large}} = 0$. $N \\equiv 0 \\pmod{32}$. ✓\n\n**Mod 3125:** $\\gcd(2016, 3125) = 1$. $\\phi(3125) = 2500$. So $N \\equiv 2016^{E_1} \\pmod{3125}$ where $E_1 = 2016^{2016^{2016}} \\mod 2500$ (reduced mod $\\phi(3125) = 2500$).\n\n$2500 = 4 \\cdot 625$, $\\gcd(4, 625) = 1$.\n\n$E_1 \\mod 4$: $2016 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$, exponent $2016^{2016} \\geq 2$, so $E_1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$.\n\n$E_1 \\mod 625$: $\\gcd(2016, 625) = 1$, $\\phi(625) = 500$. $E_1 \\equiv 2016^{E_2} \\pmod{625}$ where $E_2 = 2016^{2016} \\mod 500$.\n\n$500 = 4 \\cdot 125$.\n\n$E_2 \\mod 4$: $2016 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$, exponent $2016 \\geq 2$, so $E_2 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$.\n\n$E_2 \\mod 125$: $\\gcd(2016, 125) = 1$, $\\phi(125) = 100$. $E_2 \\equiv 2016^{2016 \\mod 100} = 2016^{16} \\pmod{125}$.\n\n$2016 \\mod 125 = 16$. $16^{16} \\mod 125$:\n\n$16^2 = 256 \\equiv 6 \\pmod{125}$.\n$16^4 \\equiv 36$.\n$16^8 \\equiv 36^2 = 1296 \\equiv 1296 - 10 \\cdot 125 = 46$.\n$16^{16} \\equiv 46^2 = 2076 \\equiv 2076 - 16 \\cdot 125 = 76$.\n\nSo $E_2 \\equiv 76 \\pmod{125}$ and $E_2 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$. $76 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$ ✓. So $E_2 \\equiv 76 \\pmod{500}$.\n\n$E_1 \\equiv 2016^{76} \\pmod{625}$. $2016 \\mod 625 = 141$. $141^{76} \\mod 625 = 16$ (computed above).\n\n$E_1 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{625}$ and $E_1 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$. $16 \\equiv 0 \\pmod 4$ ✓. So $E_1 \\equiv 16 \\pmod{2500}$.\n\n$N \\equiv 2016^{16} \\pmod{3125} = 2366$ (computed above).\n\nCRT: $N \\equiv 0 \\pmod{32}$, $N \\equiv 2366 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$N = 32k$, $32k \\equiv 2366 \\pmod{3125}$, $k \\equiv 293 \\cdot 2366 \\equiv 2613 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$N = 32 \\cdot 2613 = 8